 "description": "Megalania (Varanus priscus), the giant extinct Australian monitor lizard, side view facing right. Same body plan as komodo_dragon drawn at the same unit scale but ~1.8x as long and much bulkier: deeper head, thicker neck and limbs, heavier tail; darker olive-brown #6a5f45 with a lighter belly, pebbly scales, small hard amber eye under a heavy brow, forked tongue. A monitor lizard, not a dinosaur. SIL-safe outline (one closed shape) for the silhouette reveal (glow_r ~1200). Anchor bottom-centre (feet on y=0), ~1700x380 (x -817..867, y -375..0).",
